# Text files are LF, in the repo and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. That covers the shell
# integration scripts (bash and zsh can't read CRLF), the patches to Ghostty (git apply needs them to match its LF
# sources), and the tests that compare text against multi-line literals in their own source. Git detects binary
# files itself and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe can misread a batch file with LF line ends.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
